      "writtenOn": "2018-07-06T07:01:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "sure, It\u0027s more clear.\n\nSince we only check the \"max_depth+1\" level in db, the max_depth_found can\u0027t be got.\nfor example, if the projects in db is like:\n\nfive level\nA - B - C - D - E\n\nthen for strict-two-level case, we only need to check if three level (A - B - C) exist. So here we can only know C exceed two level, but we don\u0027t know whether D or E is behind it. Get the max depth in db will cast more time which is unnecessary.",
